40,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"My findings suggest a clear trade-off. Hardware-based holdings require expensive, time-consuming outside appraisals at quarter-end, but they offer verifiable data. Software holdings are easier to audit initially but rely entirely on their own reported figures.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"My findings indicate a significant imbalance in our human resources. While we have capacity for software-related guidance, our ability to quickly fill specialized operational or field roles is quite limited, which could create a bottleneck.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems some of our friends are more loyal than others. I found that while some services are held dear even when prices rise, others are let go quite easily. It is a gentle reminder of true value.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The financial reality is concerning. Our reserves are being depleted by follow-on calls at twice the projected rate, and our credit line is only useful for physical stock, not software contracts. We must prioritize stability.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The data is quite telling. We have a systemic risk where specific sectors—particularly those handling sensitive data or physical hardware—face massive, unpredictable delays. It's not about the team's effort, but the environment they operate in.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Misaki, if our credit line is limited to physical stock, that complicates things. However, we must weigh that against the audit burden. Hardware adds significant costs and six weeks of delay to our closing process.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mizuki, the audit burden is a concern, but we must also consider the human cost. If we choose a hardware-heavy path, we may find ourselves unable to staff the necessary field roles in a timely manner.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"It is so important to listen to these concerns. I noticed that some of our holdings struggle with delivery delays, while others are loved enough that their customers stay even when costs increase. Perhaps we should seek that kind of lasting bond.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Mizuki, the audit burden is a secondary concern compared to our liquidity. If we invest in software, we gain no borrowing power from our credit line, and our reserves are already draining faster than planned.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, you're prioritizing liquidity, but liquidity is useless if the product is stuck in a security review for nine months. We need to avoid sectors where the ""first customer"" is a myth for three quarters.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Misaki, I understand the liquidity pressure, but we cannot ignore the reporting chaos. If we add more hardware, our quarter-end becomes an expensive nightmare. However, software's lack of independent verification is a risk I can't ignore.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, your point about deployment delays is valid. However, if we choose a path that requires specialized field crews or supervisors, we risk a different kind of stall—one where we simply cannot find the people to execute.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Shizue,,It is a bit sad to see so much worry. Perhaps we can find a path that offers both the stability Misaki seeks and the genuine customer love that ensures a company's long-term health.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Shizue, love is not a hedge against insolvency. If we continue to ignore the burn rate and the limitations of our credit line, we won't have a fund left to support anyone. We need assets we can borrow against.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, borrowing against assets is a fine strategy, provided those assets actually reach the market. I'm not interested in a ""stable"" investment that spends a year in a security review before it even starts.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems we are at an impasse between liquidity, speed, and reporting. I'll be weighing the cost of those six-week audit delays against the risk of trusting unverified software dashboards when the candidates are revealed.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I will be looking for a candidate whose staffing needs align with our current capacity. We have the expertise for software, but we lack the speed to fill operational field roles. Let us hope for a balanced path.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I shall keep a gentle heart and a watchful eye. I hope we can find a candidate whose value is so genuine that their customers will stay by their side, regardless of the challenges we face.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I will be looking for a candidate with tangible assets. Given our current reserve depletion, we cannot afford another investment that offers no collateral for our credit line. Financial survival must come first.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Shion,,I'll be looking for the path of least resistance. I want a candidate that avoids both the hardware supply chain traps and the regulatory purgatory of sensitive data. Speed to market is the only real security.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
