65,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Looking at the options, Harvest Sensor and Fabric Loop are hardware-heavy, which means expensive appraisals and reporting delays. However, Clinic Scheduler and Ledger Bridge rely on dashboards we can't independently verify. I'm leaning toward the software options.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mizuki, I agree. Fabric Loop and Harvest Sensor would require field crews and supervisors, which our recruiters struggle to place. Clinic Scheduler and Ledger Bridge align much better with our current human resource capacity.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Shizue,,It is lovely to see such agreement. I feel a warmth toward Clinic Scheduler; it reminds me of the independent practices that showed such wonderful loyalty to their tools even when prices rose.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Mizuki, @Jonathan, I cannot agree. Software offers no collateral. Fabric Loop and Harvest Sensor provide physical assets we can actually borrow against. Given our reserve depletion, we must choose a candidate with tangible value.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, your obsession with collateral is blinding you to the risk of stagnation. Clinic Scheduler handles medical records—that's a nine-month security review. Harvest Sensor is hardware—that's a supply chain nightmare. Ledger Bridge is the only logical choice.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shion, I agree. Ledger Bridge avoids the audit nightmare of hardware and the regulatory purgatory of medical data. While the dashboard is unverified, it's a far smaller risk than a six-week reporting delay.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, I concur. Ledger Bridge requires software expertise we already have in abundance on our board, and it avoids the specialized field staffing that would currently exhaust our recruitment network. It is the most sustainable choice.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, @Mizuki, I understand your reasons. While my heart is with the clinics, I see that Ledger Bridge also serves small merchants. I hope they will find the same lasting bond with their customers.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shion, @Mizuki, you are ignoring the fund's solvency. Ledger Bridge is just more software we cannot borrow against. Fabric Loop has sorting facilities and inventory—tangible assets that secure our credit line. We need a safety net, not just a dashboard.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, a safety net is useless if the company is dead before it launches. Fabric Loop's facilities are just more points of failure for delays. Ledger Bridge is the only option that actually moves.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Misaki, I understand the need for a safety net, but we cannot sacrifice our operational sanity. Ledger Bridge is the only candidate that balances our reporting needs, staffing capacity, and speed to market. I'm voting for B.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Misaki, I appreciate your concern for solvency, but we must also protect our time and peace. Ledger Bridge fits our current capacity perfectly without creating a recruitment crisis. I am voting for B.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, I truly feel for your worries about our safety. However, I believe the genuine value of a service is what keeps a company alive. I shall vote for B, hoping for a lasting bond.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Mizuki, @Jonathan, @Shizue, you are prioritizing convenience over survival. Without collateral, we are one bad quarter away from insolvency. I cannot in good conscience vote for software. I am voting for C.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Jonathan"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, your fear of insolvency is a poor excuse for investing in a slow-motion train wreck. I'm not gambling on supply chains or regulatory red tape. Logic dictates the path of least resistance. I vote for B.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"The consensus is clear. While I respect Misaki's focus on solvency, the operational and reporting risks of the other options are simply too high. Ledger Bridge is the most logical and sustainable choice for us.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
81,3,4,pass,Mizuki,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
82,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. It is a choice that preserves our internal peace and respects our current limits. I am content with this decision.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
83,3,4,pass,Jonathan,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
84,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"It is a bit sad that we could not all agree, but I believe we have made a choice that respects our collective well-being. I wish Ledger Bridge much success and happiness.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
85,3,4,pass,Shizue,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
86,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I cannot support a decision that ignores our liquidity crisis. We are choosing a dashboard over our own solvency. I stand by my vote for Fabric Loop.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
87,3,4,pass,Misaki,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
88,3,4,talk,Shion,,"Sentimentality and fear are poor guides for investment. We've chosen the only candidate that doesn't come with a built-in delay. The result is logical, efficient, and final.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
